# solarized-light — Solarized, light, by Ethan Schoonover.
#
# Upstream: https://github.com/altercation/solarized
# Licence:  MIT
#
# The eight accents are byte-identical to solarized-dark. That is upstream's
# central claim, not an oversight here: the accents were picked to hold the same
# perceived relationship against either ground, so the light and dark variants
# differ ONLY in which end of the base03..base3 monotone ramp is the background.

# -- neutrals: the same monotone ramp, read from the other end --------------
COOL_BG0=#FDF6E3          # base3
COOL_BG1=#EEE8D5          # base2
COOL_BG2=#93A1A1          # base1
COOL_FG0=#586E75          # base01, the emphasised body text
COOL_FG1=#657B83          # base00
COOL_DIM=#839496          # base0
COOL_DIMMER=#93A1A1       # base1
# -- the ramp: identical to solarized-dark ----------------------------------
COOL_0=#2AA198
COOL_1=#268BD2
COOL_2=#6C71C4
COOL_3=#D33682
COOL_4=#CB4B16
# -- alert pair -------------------------------------------------------------
COOL_HOT_0=#2AA198
COOL_HOT_4=#DC322F
# -- off-ramp tints ---------------------------------------------------------
COOL_MINT=#859900
COOL_BLUSH=#D33682
# -- semantic aliases -------------------------------------------------------
COOL_ACCENT=#2AA198       # cyan
COOL_ACTIVE=#268BD2       # blue
COOL_URGENT=#DC322F       # red
COOL_WARN=#B58900         # yellow
COOL_GOOD=#859900         # green
COOL_INACTIVE=#93A1A1     # base1
